    "notes": [
      "Single-printer intaglio shop. The etching press is the nucleus: bed runs east-west, spoked wheel on the near side, crank stance kept empty.",
      "Inking slab (glass on a raised table) sits east of the press with a 1.2 m aisle. Paper soaking, flat files, and portfolios stay on the back wall, clear of ink and of the ferric cart.",
      "Two drying racks face the open front so hanging prints read from the default and corner cameras. Wash alcove is on the east wall, downstream of the paper.",
      "Dining chair faces +Z at rotation 0 (back bars measured at local -Z). Bookcase back panel is local +Z, so rotation PI opens toward the room. Chalkboard is thin in local X; rotation -PI/2 turns the writing face toward +Z. Banker's lamp shade sits on local -Z; rotation PI aims it across the slab. Long table's long axis is X and its front legs are +Z."
    ]
  },
